 lawTitle:"How this ledger maps to Japanese tax rules",
 law:["<b>Blue or white return</b>: both work. A blue return gives up to ¥650,000 deduction but needs double-entry books, which this ledger keeps. A white return only needs simple records; switch the return type in Settings and the summary follows the 収支内訳書.","<b>Double-entry, tax-inclusive</b>: each receipt becomes a debit/credit entry. Paid with personal money → credit 事業主借 (owner's contribution). Paid from the business account with a private share → the private part goes to 事業主貸 (owner's drawings).","<b>Business-use ratio (家事按分)</b>: for phone, rent and similar, only the business share is expensed.","<b>Invoice system</b>: a T + 13-digit registration number marks the receipt as qualified. Under standard taxation, non-qualified purchases are 50% deductible from 2026-10-01 to 2029-09-30 (80% before).","<b>Electronic Bookkeeping Act</b>: receipt photos are kept with the books and searchable by date, amount and vendor (the Journal filters). Every edit or deletion is logged in the database (訂正削除履歴). Keep records for 7 years.","Depreciation (assets ¥100,000+), inventory and withholding tax are not calculated here. Supplies of ¥100,000 or more are flagged."],
